# Courier kit fit

This review is limited to the courier assembly and the pinned component contracts. It is not an external steward response or an execution result.

- **Courier configuration and rules:** The existing scaffold courier factory composes grid-map with engine-core and game-store. The game supplies its board, locations, allowances and authored route. No additional engine, card language, combat, payment or campaign subsystem is needed. Keep the independent seven-rule inventory and the refusal/boundary fixtures separate from the executable handler code.
- **Screen: courier board:** Existing app-frame, screens, settings and saves own navigation and forms. The game supplies its board-cell view, status text and minimal tokens. Plain-text checks mounted content; theme-check checks authored tokens and supplies browser measurements. A successful static or jsdom check does not establish browser layout correctness.

The strict plan profile explicitly excludes cards and an LLM playtester because this original example has neither. It retains structural, scenario, session, reuse and applicable test-depth checks. The plan does not use legacy optional flags or pretend to implement an architect wrapper.
